description:
Combined vk23 audit follow-up.

The generated mechanics projection for creature recharge abilities appears to parse ranges like "Recharge 5–6" and "Recharge 4–6" incorrectly by setting maximum equal to the lower bound.

Examples observed in the vk23 audit bundle:
- creature:adult-red-dragon — Fire Breath (Recharge 5–6) projected as { roll: "d6", minimum: 5, maximum: 5 }
- creature:ancient-red-dragon — Fire Breath (Recharge 5–6) projected as { roll: "d6", minimum: 5, maximum: 5 }
- creature:air-elemental — Whirlwind (Recharge 4–6) projected as { roll: "d6", minimum: 4, maximum: 4 }
- creature:blink-dog — Teleport (Recharge 4–6) projected as { roll: "d6", minimum: 4, maximum: 4 }
- creature:water-elemental — Whelm (Recharge 4–6) projected as { roll: "d6", minimum: 4, maximum: 4 }

This is not a source-coverage failure, but it is a deterministic gameplay bug: combat automation would under-trigger recharge abilities.

Acceptance criteria:
- Parse "Recharge N–6" as minimum N and maximum 6, preserving the correct d6 recharge threshold.
- Add regression coverage for at least Recharge 5–6 and Recharge 4–6 examples.
- Verify affected generated creature records regenerate with the correct recharge range.
- Ensure verify:dnd5e-srd-pack remains byte-clean after regeneration.
